    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6943": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer, Molecular Biology",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer, Molecular Biology - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Senior Lecturer, Molecular Biology Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role We are seeking an outstanding academic to advance the University of Wollongong's leadership in the emerging field of Quantum Biotechnology. Working across the School of Science and Molecular Horizons you will develop a high-impact research program at the interface of quantum science and the life sciences, contributing to interdisciplinary collaboration, research excellence and external funding success. You will also deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate programs in chemistry, biochemistry and molecular biology, including subject coordination, curriculum development, and incorporation of research-led teaching practices, and play an active role in academic leadership, governance and engagement activities across the University. Key responsibilities: Lead impactful research in Quantum Biotechnology; Collaborate within the University of Wollongong and   through the ARC Centre of Excellence in Quantum Biotechnology (QUBIC); Attract research funding and publish high-quality research; Supervise research students and early-career researchers; Deliver innovative teaching and curriculum development; and Contribute to academic leadership and service. About the Team The School of Science (SSCI) teaches and conducts research in Biomedical Sciences including Biochemistry, Molecular Biophysics, Microbiology and Cell and Molecular Biology, all disciplines of Chemistry including Atmospheric, Medicinal and Environmental Chemistry, as well as Conservation Biology, Earth Surface Processes, Ecology, Ecotoxicology, Environmental Science, Earth systems, Marine Biology and Spatial Sciences. SSCI has a global research presence facilitated by its strengths in both the Molecular Horizons Research Institute and Environmental Futures Centre. SSCI staff have global research connections providing multi-faceted opportunities for knowledge growth and development. What You’ll Bring A PhD in physics, chemistry, biophysics, biochemistry, molecular biology or a related discipline; Demonstrated expertise in Quantum Biotechnology, for example in the fields of Molecular Qubits, Quantum Sensing, and Protein Engineering. A strong record of research excellence and scholarly impact; The ability to attract research funding and develop collaborative partnerships; Experience mentoring and supervising emerging researchers; A passion for delivering engaging teaching and learning experiences; and A collaborative mindset and enthusiasm for interdisciplinary research. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas and New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Permanent/Continuing | Full-time appointment Level C: $151,746 - $171,141 + 17% Superannuation Position Description Location: Wollongong Camus How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be prompted to respond to a selection criteria questionnaire as part of the application process. Please also attach your CV to your application. For further information about this position, please contact Professor Martina Sanderson-Smith, Acting Head, School of Science via email: ssci-admin@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Tuesday 13 October 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated.  We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University’s employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. About Us At the University of Wollongong (UOW) , our people are united by a shared purpose — to create a better future through education, research, innovation and meaningful community impact. With deep local roots and a growing global presence, UOW is proud to contribute to positive change in the communities we serve and the world beyond them. Guided by our Vision 2035 and Strategic Plan 2030 , we are building a future that is innovative, inclusive and committed to societal impact — one where people, ideas and opportunity can thrive. We are recognised for excellence in teaching and research, and for the real-world impact of our work. But what truly brings UOW to life is our people. Across every role, our staff contribute to something bigger — helping shape the future through the work they do every day. At UOW, we are committed to fostering a culture where people feel valued, supported and empowered to do their best work. Our Values in Action guide how we work, lead and make decisions — creating a workplace grounded in integrity, accountability, collaboration and excellence. Joining UOW means becoming part of a values-led community where your work has purpose, your contribution is valued, and the impact you make can be felt locally and globally. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6943 Job Category Academia Posting Date 09/10/2026, 10:44 PM Apply Before 10/13/2026, 05:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs Lecturer or Senior Lecturer, Psychiatry Wollongong, NSW, Australia Posted on 08/14/2026 Graduate School of Medicine | Faculty of Science, Medicine and Health Lecturer or Senior Lecturer Wollongong, NSW, Australia Posted on 08/26/2026 School of Social Sciences | Faculty of Arts, Society and Business See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Senior Lecturer, Molecular Biology - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
