    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6986": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Manager: Cryo-electron Microscopy",
      "description": "Senior Technical Manager: Cryo-electron Microscopy - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Senior Technical Manager: Cryo-electron Microscopy Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW), a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The Senior Technical Manager: Cryo-electron Microscopy plays a critical leadership role within UOW Research Infrastructure's CryoEM Facility, supporting world-class research outcomes through specialist technical expertise, facility management and user support. The role provides advanced training and technical services to researchers, students and external partners, while overseeing the operation, optimisation and future development of cutting-edge cryoEM instrumentation and workflows. Key responsibilities: Lead the day-to-day operation, maintenance and optimisation of the CryoEM facility and associated instrumentation. Deliver expert training and support to internal and external users across cryoEM workflows, from sample preparation through to data analysis and structure determination. Develop, implement and enhance computational cryoEM processing workflows and data acquisition methods. Collaborate with researchers on experimental design, data collection and research projects in cryoEM structural biology. Supervise staff, manage facility access, and contribute to stakeholder engagement, reporting and scientific outputs. About the Team The position sits within UOW Research Infrastructure, a newly established strategic division within the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research and Innovation) Portfolio. The team provides leadership and oversight of major research facilities and infrastructure across the University, ensuring researchers have access to high-quality, sustainable and impactful capabilities. Working closely with researchers, students, industry partners and external stakeholders, the CryoEM Facility supports cutting-edge research that advances scientific discovery and innovation. What You'll Bring Extensive hands-on experience in cryo-electron microscopy workflows, including sample preparation, image analysis and particle reconstruction. Demonstrated expertise operating, aligning, calibrating and troubleshooting advanced cryoEM platforms and associated automation software. Strong experience with contemporary cryoEM data processing platforms and high-performance computing environments. Proven ability to design, manage and deliver complex scientific projects, coupled with excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills. Experience leading or supervising staff within a research, technical or laboratory environment. A PhD in Biochemistry, Biology or a related discipline would be highly regarded. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type : Continuing, full-time Level: 8/9 | $123,283 - $152,959 + 17% superannuation Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. This position is not suitable for remote working arrangements. Position Description How to Apply Click on the 'Apply Now' button at the bottom of the advertisement. You'll be prompted to respond to a selection criteria questionnaire as part of the application process. Please also attach your CV to your application. For further information about this position, please contact Simon Brown, Senior Manager – Microscopy Facility simonb@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Tuesday 13 October 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender Based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender Based Violence during previous employment or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University's employment screening processes and treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. About Us At the University of Wollongong (UOW) , our people are united by a shared purpose — to create a better future through education, research, innovation and meaningful community impact. With deep local roots and a growing global presence, UOW is proud to contribute to positive change in the communities we serve and the world beyond them. Guided by our Vision 2035 and Strategic Plan 2030 , we are building a future that is innovative, inclusive and committed to societal impact — one where people, ideas and opportunity can thrive. We are recognised for excellence in teaching and research, and for the real-world impact of our work. But what truly brings UOW to life is our people. Across every role, our staff contribute to something bigger — helping shape the future through the work they do every day. At UOW, we are committed to fostering a culture where people feel valued, supported and empowered to do their best work. Our Values in Action guide how we work, lead and make decisions — creating a workplace grounded in integrity, accountability, collaboration and excellence. Joining UOW means becoming part of a values-led community where your work has purpose, your contribution is valued, and the impact you make can be felt locally and globally. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6986 Job Category Academic Enablement Posting Date 09/21/2026, 11:21 PM Apply Before 10/13/2026, 05:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs Program Manager – IDAM Wollongong, NSW, Australia Posted on 09/03/2026 This 16-month contract opportunity will lead the delivery of the University's Identity and Access Management (IDAM) Program, a major cyber security initiative aimed at modernising how users access systems and information across the University. Lecturer or Senior Lecturer, Psychiatry Wollongong, NSW, Australia Posted on 08/14/2026 Graduate School of Medicine | Faculty of Science, Medicine and Health See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Senior Technical Manager: Cryo-electron Microscopy - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
