    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6987": {
      "title": "Technical Officer: Cryo-electron Microscopy",
      "description": "Technical Officer: Cryo-electron Microscopy - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Technical Officer: Cryo-electron Microscopy Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW), a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The Technical Officer: Cryo-electron Microscopy provides specialist technical expertise within UOW Research Infrastructure’s CryoEM Facility, supporting high-quality research through training, technical services and hands-on user support. Focusing on single particle CryoEM, you will work closely with researchers, students and external stakeholders across workflows from sample preparation and data acquisition through to analysis and structure determination. Working alongside senior facility staff, you will also support the day-to-day operation of the facility, including equipment maintenance and calibration, workflow testing, troubleshooting, benchmarking and laboratory management. Key responsibilities: Deliver specialist training and hands-on support to internal and external users across single particle CryoEM workflows. Assist researchers with sample preparation, data acquisition and data interrogation. Undertake routine maintenance, calibration and benchmarking of CryoEM equipment and workflows. Troubleshoot instrumentation and liaise with manufacturers and service providers as required. Test and optimise microscopy and data analysis workflows. Support the effective operation of laboratory spaces, including consumables management and maintaining safety requirements to PC2 standards. About the Team The position sits within UOW Research Infrastructure, a newly established strategic division within the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research and Innovation) Portfolio. The team provides leadership and oversight of major research facilities and infrastructure across the University, ensuring researchers have access to high-quality, sustainable and impactful capabilities. Working closely with researchers, students, industry partners and external stakeholders, the CryoEM Facility supports cutting-edge research and provides specialist expertise and infrastructure to advance scientific discovery and innovation. What You’ll Bring Demonstrated technical expertise and hands-on experience with cryo-electron microscopy instrumentation in a research environment. Experience across single particle CryoEM workflows, including sample preparation, data acquisition and data interrogation. Demonstrated ability to train and support a diverse range of users, from students through to experienced researchers and subject matter experts. An understanding of PC2 laboratory requirements, WHS principles and risk management within a laboratory environment. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a genuine enthusiasm for supporting research and development. The ability to engage effectively with researchers, academics, industry partners and suppliers and work successfully within a university research environment. Knowledge of biochemistry and molecular biology and/or a PhD in Biochemistry, Biology or a related discipline would be highly regarded. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Continuing, full-time (35 hours per week) Level: 6/7 | 96,898 - $119,986 + 17% superannuation Location: Wollongong Campus Manual handling and lifting may be required from time to time. Position Description How to Apply Click on the 'Apply Now' button at the bottom of the advertisement. You'll be prompted to respond to a selection criteria questionnaire as part of the application process. Please also attach your CV to your application. For further information about this position, please contact Simon Brown, Senior Manager – Microscopy Facility simonb@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Thursday, 15 October 2026 11:59 PM Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender Based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender Based Violence during previous employment or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University's employment screening processes and treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. About Us At the University of Wollongong (UOW) , our people are united by a shared purpose — to create a better future through education, research, innovation and meaningful community impact. With deep local roots and a growing global presence, UOW is proud to contribute to positive change in the communities we serve and the world beyond them. Guided by our Vision 2035 and Strategic Plan 2030 , we are building a future that is innovative, inclusive and committed to societal impact — one where people, ideas and opportunity can thrive. We are recognised for excellence in teaching and research, and for the real-world impact of our work. But what truly brings UOW to life is our people. Across every role, our staff contribute to something bigger — helping shape the future through the work they do every day. At UOW, we are committed to fostering a culture where people feel valued, supported and empowered to do their best work. Our Values in Action guide how we work, lead and make decisions — creating a workplace grounded in integrity, accountability, collaboration and excellence. Joining UOW means becoming part of a values-led community where your work has purpose, your contribution is valued, and the impact you make can be felt locally and globally. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6987 Job Category Academic Enablement Posting Date 09/23/2026, 08:20 PM Apply Before 10/15/2026, 05:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Technical Officer: Cryo-electron Microscopy - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
