    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/7012": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Academic Leader, Indigenous Health) Identified*",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Academic Leader, Indigenous Health) Identified* - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Associate Professor (Academic Leader, Indigenous Health) Identified* Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role Lead and advance Indigenous Health education, research and student success within UOW’s Doctor of Medicine program. Working collaboratively across the University, health services and Indigenous communities you will drive curriculum innovation, support Indigenous student pathways and strengthen Indigenous health outcomes through teaching, research and strategic leadership. Key responsibilities: Work collaboratively with GSM and UOW to ensure the GSM MD program is accredited by the Australian Medical Council (AMC) and addresses all accreditation requirements Lead the Indigenous Health team in its strategies to increase Indigenous student recruitment and retention, improve the Indigenous Health curriculum and support UOW staff to address equity matters in relation to Indigenous staff and students Lead the development and delivery of Indigenous Health curriculum, teaching and assessment within the MD program Build and strengthen partnerships with Indigenous communities, health services and key stakeholders Support the recruitment, retention and success of Indigenous medical students Provide leadership, mentoring and support to Indigenous staff and students Contribute to Indigenous Health research, accreditation activities and strategic initiatives across the program About the Team The Graduate School of Medicine (GSM) is committed to engaging with and responding to the health and workforce needs of our local, regional, and rural communities. Our goal is to improve health and wellbeing through excellence in medical education and meaningful, community-focused research.  Our graduates become skilled, compassionate practitioners committed to improving healthcare, especially in regional, rural, and remote communities. Our research and teaching tackle health inequities, strengthen wellbeing in underserved areas, and support Indigenous-led initiatives shaped by Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander priorities. What You’ll Bring An understanding of AMC processes, changes to its Medical School Accreditation Standards and conditions to improve Medical Programs A passion for advancing Indigenous Health education, research and outcomes Strong connections with Indigenous communities and a commitment to culturally safe practice Experience in teaching, curriculum development and student support Research expertise or an emerging research profile in Indigenous Health The ability to build meaningful partnerships and inspire others through collaboration and leadership Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation UOW is committed to equality, diversity and inclusion and strives to be an employer of choice for Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Australians Generous working conditions in a great location, with sociable hours, family friendly policies, flexible work practices and culturally sensitive leave provisions, including cultural and ceremonial leave Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Continuing Contingent* | Full-time appointment Level D: $183,028 - $196,423 + 17% Superannuation Location: Based at Wollongong campus, with occasional travel to Shoalhaven and Southern Highlands campuses Additional Information *This is an Identified position. The University of Wollongong (UOW) considers that being an Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander is a genuine occupational qualification for this position under s14 of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 (NSW). Current Australian Driver’s License required Ability to meet NSW Health vaccination requirements for work within public health facilities. This position is subject to a National Criminal Check. Position Description How to Apply To apply for this position, you are required to submit a resume, and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Professor Zsuzsoka Kecskes, Dean of Medicine via email: zkecskes@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Sunday 25 October 2026, 11:55pm *Continuing Contingent: Refer to section 21 of the University of Wollongong (Academic Staff) Enterprise Agreement, 2023:   This position forms part of an external funding agreement. Should funding cease and not be renewed Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated.  We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University’s employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation . About Us At the University of Wollongong (UOW) , our people are united by a shared purpose — to create a better future through education, research, innovation and meaningful community impact. With deep local roots and a growing global presence, UOW is proud to contribute to positive change in the communities we serve and the world beyond them. Guided by our Vision 2035 and Strategic Plan 2030 , we are building a future that is innovative, inclusive and committed to societal impact — one where people, ideas and opportunity can thrive. We are recognised for excellence in teaching and research, and for the real-world impact of our work. But what truly brings UOW to life is our people. Across every role, our staff contribute to something bigger — helping shape the future through the work they do every day. At UOW, we are committed to fostering a culture where people feel valued, supported and empowered to do their best work. Our Values in Action guide how we work, lead and make decisions — creating a workplace grounded in integrity, accountability, collaboration and excellence. Joining UOW means becoming part of a values-led community where your work has purpose, your contribution is valued, and the impact you make can be felt locally and globally. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 7012 Job Category Academia Posting Date 09/27/2026, 04:54 PM Apply Before 10/25/2026, 05:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by 