    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6993": {
      "title": "Technology Officer",
      "description": "Technology Officer - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Technology Officer Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role Play a key role in supporting the Graduate School of Medicine's educational technology systems that underpin the Doctor of Medicine (MD) program. You'll lead the implementation, administration and continuous improvement of specialist medical education platforms, working closely with academic, clinical and professional staff to deliver effective, secure and user-focused technology solutions across multiple campuses and clinical training sites. Key responsibilities: Support the implementation and administration of key medical education systems Provide support and guidance to staff using educational technologies Develop resources and processes that improve the user experience. Identify and implement system improvements through feedback and evaluation Collaborate with stakeholders to support technology initiatives and accreditation requirements About the Team The Graduate School of Medicine (GSM) is part of the Faculty of Science, Medicine and Health and delivers UOW's Doctor of Medicine program across Wollongong, Shoalhaven, Southern Highlands and a network of rural clinical sites throughout NSW. The team is committed to improving health and wellbeing through excellence in medical education and works closely with academic, clinical and professional partners to support future medical practitioners. What You’ll Bring Relevant qualifications or equivalent experience in information technology Experience supporting education or clinical technology systems Strong stakeholder engagement and communication skills The ability to coordinate projects and manage competing priorities A collaborative, solutions-focused approach to problem solving Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas and New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Fixed-term | Part-time (21 hours per week, 0.6 FTE, Monday to Wednesday) to 31 December 2027 Level 5: $85,682 - $96,898 (pro-rata) + 17% Superannuation Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required.  Visa sponsorship is not available This position may only be suitable for remote working arrangements on occasion, or outside of student session Position Description How to Apply To apply for this position, click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be prompted to respond to a selection criteria questionnaire as part of the application process. Please also attach your CV to your application. For further information about this position, please contact Christie Goodisson, GSM School Operations Manager via email cgoodisson@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Sunday 25 October 2026, 11:55pm The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated.  We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of