    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/7064": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Senior Executive Assistant - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Senior Executive Assistant Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Senior Executive Assistant Vice-Chancellor’s Unit | University of Wollongong Level 6/7 Wollongong Campus Are you an experienced executive support professional who thrives in a fast-paced environment and enjoys working with senior leaders? The University of Wollongong (UOW) is seeking a highly organised and proactive Senior Executive Assistant to join our Vice-Chancellor’s Unit. This is an opportunity to work at the heart of the University, providing high-level, confidential executive and administrative support to our senior leadership team. You will play an important role in ensuring the smooth operation of executive offices, supporting University governance and building strong relationships with a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders. About the role Working in a dynamic and collaborative environment, you will exercise sound judgement, initiative and discretion to manage competing priorities and deliver exceptional executive support. Your key responsibilities will include: Providing high-level executive support, including complex diary management, correspondence, briefings and confidential documentation. Coordinating domestic and international travel, high-profile events and visiting delegations. Building and maintaining effective relationships with senior executives, Council members, government representatives and external partners. Providing cross-functional support across senior executive offices to ensure continuity of service. Supporting University governance, committees and strategic projects. Identifying opportunities to improve administrative systems, processes and service delivery. About you You are a confident and resourceful professional with exceptional organisational and communication skills. You enjoy working collaboratively, anticipate the needs of senior leaders and remain calm and effective under pressure. You will bring: At least five years' experience providing high-level executive support, preferably within a large and complex organisation. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage professionally and diplomatically with stakeholders at all levels. Exceptional attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities and tight deadlines. Demonstrated initiative, sound judgement and discretion when handling sensitive and confidential matters. Strong problem-solving skills and a commitment to continuous improvement. A collaborative, flexible approach and a willingness to support colleagues across executive portfolios. A relevant degree or equivalent combination of education, training and experience is required. Experience in higher education, governance or government relations will be highly regarded. Why join UOW? At UOW, you will be part of a supportive and collaborative team that works closely with the University's senior leadership. You will have the opportunity to contribute to meaningful initiatives, engage with a diverse range of stakeholders and support the University's strategic priorities. We are guided by our Values in Action: Thrive Together, Pursue Excellence, Be Accountable and Lead with Integrity. Role Details Employment type : Permanent/Continuing | Full-time Level 6/7 | $96,898 - $119,986 + 17% superannuation. Position Description Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required.  Visa sponsorship is not available. How to apply To apply, please submit your resume and a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and suitability for the position. For further information please contact Marcia Sherlock marciac@uow.edu.au or +61 2 4221 5923. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 7064 Job Category Administration Posting Date 10/05/2026, 05:40 PM Apply Before 10/18/2026, 05:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Senior Executive Assistant - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
